.TH "SKARN-EXPORT" "1" "2026-06-23" "skarn 0.17.2" "Skarn Manual"
.SH NAME
skarn\-export \- Export sessions as text, json, ndjson, or html (redacted by
default)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskarn\fR \fBexport\fR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Export sessions as text, json, ndjson, or html (redacted by default).
.PP
Export session data.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-cli\fR \fIname\fR
Restrict to one assistant's sessions. One of: claude, gemini, codex, cursor,
copilot.
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fIpath\fR
Restrict to sessions whose project path contains this substring.
.TP
\fB\-\-worktree\fR \fIpath\fR
Restrict to sessions whose working directory is under this path.
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fIdate\fR
Lower bound of the time window; takes priority over \-\-hours.
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fIdate\fR
Upper bound of the time window.
.TP
\fB\-\-tz\-offset\fR \fIminutes\fR
Timezone offset in minutes for date grouping and display. The default is 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-hours\fR \fIn\fR
Time window in hours; 0 means no limit. The default is 168.
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fIid\fR
Restrict to a single session by id (prefix\-matched).
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIfmt\fR
Output format. One of: text, json, ndjson, html. The default is text.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-redact\fR
Emit raw session content; by default every detected secret is redacted.
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fIfile\fR
Write to this file instead of stdout.
.TP
\fB\-\-open\fR
Open the written file in the default viewer (needs \-\-out).
.TP
\fB\-\-gzip\fR
Gzip\-compress the output (needs \-\-out, or \-\-format html).
